From 0a1c90bd4c6141c705cb8438f93f0bb72f97b245 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Levine <blahm1d@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 01:04:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] core: P0004 (JRP condition) + P0005 (SRL/SRA K-form
 shift amount)

Two more real TMS34010 core bugs found running Smash T.V. attract code (MAME
golden-reference method). Both documented in PATCHES.md.

- P0004: jump condition code 0001 is P (positive, ~N & ~Z), not CC_LO (st_c).
  The core mislabeled/evaluated it as unsigned-lower (which is really code 1000
  = CC_C). Every JRP branched on the wrong flag. Fixed the enum + evaluator +
  decoder accepted-set. Verified vs MAME (line-draw step sign +1, loop terminates).
- P0005: SRL/SRA K-form encodes the count as 2's-complement (32-amount); the core
  passed the raw k5 for the K-form (only the Rs-form was complemented), so
  "SRL 1Ch" shifted right by 4 instead of 28. Fixed. Verified vs MAME (DYDX
  assembles to 0x00080006; the draw loop now renders 231 attract objects).

