+
+## P0004 — JRP condition code mislabeled CC_LO (branches wrong)
+
+**Status:** ✅ APPLIED + VERIFIED 2026-07-05. `grep -rn P0004 rtl/`.
+
+**Applied edits (all in the vendored core):**
+- `rtl/tms34010_pkg.sv`: `CC_LO = 4'b0001` → **`CC_P = 4'b0001`** (comment fixed).
+- `rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv` (branch evaluator): `CC_LO: branch_taken = st_c;`
+  → **`CC_P: branch_taken = !st_n & !st_z;`** (P = positive, ~N & ~Z).
+- `rtl/core/tms34010_decode.sv` (3 accepted-set lists): `CC_LO` → `CC_P`.
+
+**Problem.** TMS34010 jump condition code `0001` is **P (positive: ~N & ~Z)**, but the
+core mapped it to `CC_LO` and evaluated it as `st_c` (unsigned-lower). "Unsigned-lower"
+(borrow) is actually code `1000` = `CC_C`. So every `JRP` branched on the wrong flag.
+
+**Evidence (real ROM + MAME).** Smash T.V. line-draw step-sign (`fff4fa00: JRP`): after
+`CMP A3,A4` (A3=`F028`, A4=`FC30`), flags are N=Z=C=V=0 in **both** MAME and our sim, but
+MAME **takes** the JRP (`P` true) and our core did not (`st_c`=0). Post-fix our core takes
+it too; the line-draw step comes out `+1` (was `-1`), matching MAME, and the boot's
+line-draw loop terminates instead of hanging.
+
+---
+
+## P0005 — SRL/SRA K-form shift by wrong amount (32-K)
+
+**Status:** ✅ APPLIED + VERIFIED 2026-07-05. `grep -rn P0005 rtl/`.
+
+**Applied edit:** `rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv` (`shifter_amount` mux) — add
+`INSTR_SRA_K, INSTR_SRL_K: shifter_amount = (~decoded.k5) + 1;` (2's complement),
+instead of falling through to `default: shifter_amount = decoded.k5;`.
+
+**Problem.** The TMS34010 `SRL`/`SRA` **K-form** encodes its count field as the
+**2's-complement (32-amount)** of the shift amount — e.g. "SRL 1Ch" (right-28) is
+opcode `0x2c85`, raw K-field `0x04` (= 32-28). The `SLL`/`SLA`/`RL` K-forms store the
+amount directly. The core 2's-complemented the *Rs*-form right shifts but passed the raw
+`k5` for the *K*-form, so `SRL K` shifted right by `32-K` (e.g. `>>28` became `>>4`).
+
+**Evidence (real ROM + MAME).** Smash T.V. sprite DYDX assembly: `SLL 1Ch,A5` →
+`0x80000000`, then `SRL 1Ch,A5`: MAME `>>28` = `0x8`, our core `>>4` = `0x08000000`.
+Post-fix `SRL 1Ch` gives `0x8` and DYDX assembles to `0x00080006` (matching MAME); the
+draw loop then renders 231 attract objects (was 1) via PIXBLT.
+
+**Upstream note (P0004+P0005).** Both are real TMS34010 core bugs — offer upstream to
+birdybro. Neither is Y-unit-specific; they only surfaced running real game code (the
+per-instruction unit TBs didn't exercise `JRP`-after-`CMP` or the `SRL` K-form encoding).
diff --git a/rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv b/rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv
index 4fd428b..3e8cb4a 100644
--- a/rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv
+++ b/rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv
@@ -2021,7 +2021,7 @@ module tms34010_core
   always_comb begin
     unique case (decoded.branch_cc)
       CC_UC:   branch_taken = 1'b1;
-      CC_LO:   branch_taken = st_c;                   // unsigned <
+      CC_P:    branch_taken = !st_n & !st_z;           // P0004: P = positive (>0), ~N & ~Z
       CC_LS:   branch_taken = st_c | st_z;             // unsigned <=
       CC_HI:   branch_taken = !st_c & !st_z;           // unsigned >
       CC_LT:   branch_taken = st_n ^ st_v;             // signed   <
@@ -2329,6 +2329,13 @@ module tms34010_core
       INSTR_SRA_RR,
       INSTR_SRL_RR: shifter_amount = (~rf_rs1_data[SHIFT_AMOUNT_WIDTH-1:0])
                                      + {{(SHIFT_AMOUNT_WIDTH-1){1'b0}}, 1'b1};
+      // P0005: the SRL/SRA K-form encodes its count as (32 - amount) — the raw
+      // 5-bit field is the 2's complement of the shift amount (e.g. "SRL 1Ch"
+      // = shift-right-28 = field 0x04). The SLL/SLA/RL K-forms store the amount
+      // directly. So right-shift-by-constant must 2's-complement k5, mirroring
+      // the Rs-form above. (Was: default -> k5, which shifted right by 32-K.)
+      INSTR_SRA_K,
+      INSTR_SRL_K:  shifter_amount = (~decoded.k5) + {{(SHIFT_AMOUNT_WIDTH-1){1'b0}}, 1'b1};
       default:      shifter_amount = decoded.k5;
     endcase
   end
